// ADR-009 C3 #14 slice 4 (S4d) — the SUGAR-DECLARED typed-config
// zero-fallback smoke, SINGLE-carrier shape: a declarative annotation with
// MIXED (int, string) config params installs a `before` hook through the
// S4c sugar lowering — minted body fn + synthesized public-API handler
// (`install(before_hook(<minted>, [capture("times", times),
// capture("tag", tag)]))`), config bound as ConstLift'd declared captures
// (C3-G4/G5) via the S4b typed injection, baked by the S3b ConstLift into
// the specialized handler's `let mut times: int = 3` / `let mut tag:
// string = "ab"` prologue constants. The mixed-type shape is EXACTLY the
// #66 item-1 capability S4a unlocked (per-call-site capture value typing).
//
// The target is 1-ary (MutationCarrier::Single) — deliberately OFF the
// known S2d aggregate-carrier gap, which stays S7's named follow-up with
// its measurement; this cell isolates sugar+mixed-config JIT behavior.
//
// STRING-CONSUMPTION SPELLING (measured S4d): the hook body consumes the
// baked string via an EQUALITY BRANCH (`if tag == "ab"`), the same spelling
// the S1a (int, string) aggregate cell proved native — a scalar-returning
// string method (`tag.length()`) instead hits the PRE-EXISTING named
// STAGE-StringJIT whole-program deopt (`jit-string-scalar-method-deopt`,
// loud surface-and-stop, unrelated to the sugar path; the in-process S4
// unit pins keep the `.length()` spelling on the VM tier).
//
// Hot loop of 200 calls crosses T1@100 (`crates/shape-vm/src/tier.rs`).
// The annotation's declarative hook and its synthesized `comptime post`
// handler are NOT top-level comptime blocks (parse-based vacuity guard in
// the cell).
//
// Value-distinguishing arithmetic, per call i in 0..200:
//   before: a0 = i * times + (tag == "ab" ? 2 : 0) = 3i + 2
//   impl:   * 10                                   → 30i + 20
//   sum = 30 * 19900 + 20 * 200 = 601000
// Expected stdout: 601000
//   skipped before               → sum 10i   = 199000
//   tag misread (branch false)   → 30i       = 597000
//   times misread as 1           → 10i + 20  = 203000
annotation boosted(times: int, tag: string) on function {
  before(args) {
    if tag == "ab" {
      args[0] = args[0] * times + 2
    } else {
      args[0] = args[0] * times
    }
    return args
  }
}

@boosted(3, "ab")
fn calc(a: int) -> int { a * 10 }

fn run() -> int {
  let mut total = 0
  for i in 0..200 { total = total + calc(i) }
  total
}
print(run())
